{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Lecturer-in-Operations-Management/44603-en_US": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Operations Management",
      "description": "Lecturer in Operations Management Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44603 Job Title: Lecturer in Operations Management City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Management & Marketing in the Doermer School of Business at Purdue University Fort Wayne (PFW) seeks a lecturer to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in areas such as operations management, supply chain management, project management, management science, and related fields. The position requires a combination of online, hybrid, and face-to-face course delivery. Additional responsibilities include developing new courses, supporting student organizations, and fulfilling standard departmental service obligations. Qualifications Candidates should hold at least a master's degree and have a major in operations management or a related field. Candidates should detail any prior teaching and/or industry experience. Candidates should maintain appropriate AACSB faculty qualifications while in the position. There is a promotion process from Lecturer to Senior Lecturer. The position begins in Fall 2027. Preferred qualifications include previous teaching experience in a university setting and/or industry experience. Application Process Upload the letter of application, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching effectiveness, a 1–2-page statement of teaching philosophy, and a copy of the graduate transcript to https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Lecturer-in-Operations-Management/44603-en_US. Please email three letters of recommendation to MGMKFS@pfw.edu. Candidates invited to a campus visit will deliver a 45-60-minute instructional presentation. For questions, contact Dr. Xiaoguang Tian, Chair of the Department of Management and Marketing at Purdue University Fort Wayne, at tianxg@pfw.edu or (260) 481-6945. Screening will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is contingent upon available funding and a satisfactory background check. PFW is an AACSB International-accredited university and an EEO/AA employer. PFW will not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/13/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology/44515-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44515 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Biology City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor with expertise in Aquatic Biology beginning August 2027. Teaching responsibilities include, but are not limited to, introductory and intermediate level undergraduate courses in ecology, upper-level aquatic biology for undergraduate majors, and an upper-level or graduate course developed based on the candidate’s area of expertise. Demonstrated experience in teaching undergraduate biology is preferred. Faculty are expected to participate in student advising as well as service to the department and university. Establishment of a funded research program involving undergraduate and M.S. graduate students is expected. Research in any area of aquatic biology will be considered. Ph.D. in Biology or closely related field is required. Position is contingent upon available funding and satisfactory background check. The Department The Department of Biological Sciences is the largest department in the College of Science with over 400 undergraduate majors and 40 graduate students. More than half of undergraduates pursue graduate or professional degrees after graduation. The department has extensive facilities for its teaching and research programs, and the 14 faculty represent specialties spanning the breadth of the discipline. The University Purdue University Fort Wayne is the largest university in northeast Indiana, offering 25 graduate and over 100 prestigious Purdue University undergraduate degrees and certificates. The 594 ‐ acre campus in Fort Wayne is home to over 7,000 degree ‐ seeking undergraduate and graduate students. PFW is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. Learn more about us at PFW.edu. Application Process Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, selected recent reprints, statements of research interests and 1-2 page teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and the names of three references to https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/go/FW-Faculty/7720100/. All candidates invited for a campus interview will be expected to conduct a 45-60 minute instructional student presentation. Candidates for this position will also be expected to provide a 45-60 minute presentation on their proposed research program and how they would incorporate undergraduate and graduate students in their research. For full consideration, apply by November 9, 2026 . Screening will continue until the position is filled. Please contact Dr. Scott Bergeson bergesos@pfw.edu with any questions. Purdue Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/12/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Mechanical-Engineering/44514-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44514 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering at Purdue University Fort Wayne (PFW) invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position in mechanical engineering starting in August 2027. Qualifications Candidates must have a Bachelor of Science degree in mechanical engineering and have earned a doctorate degree in mechanical engineering or a closely related area by the time of appointment.  This position will require teaching and research. Successful candidates will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the general area of mechanical engineering, particularly the mechanics area, as well as engineering fundamentals within the First-Year Engineering program.  Applicants for the position are required to have a strong commitment to teaching and laboratory instruction.  Candidates shall have the ability to establish and sustain an active research program in their area of expertise and to attract external funding that leads to publications in scholarly journals. Candidates are also expected to participate in service activities at the academic, professional, and/or community levels. PFW offers a competitive salary and benefits package and an excellent work environment. Fort Wayne is the second largest city in Indiana and is located within a few hours of drive time to Chicago, Columbus, Cleveland, Cincinnati, Detroit, and Indianapolis. It is a great community that boasts affordable housing and a low cost of living. Application Process philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, research plan, and the names of three references to https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Mechanical-Engineering/44514-en_US . Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position has been filled. All candidates who are interviewed will be asked to prepare and deliver a 40-minute teaching demonstration. Purdue University Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer. The position is contingent on available funding and a satisfactory background records check. Candidates must be allowed to work in the US by the start date. Should you have questions, please contact the Search Committee Chair: Dr. Hosni Abu-Mulaweh Purdue University Fort Wayne Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering 2101 East Coliseum Boulevard Fort Wayne, IN 46805-1499 MESearch@pfw.edu https://www.pfw.edu/etcs/cme Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/8/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Psychology/40108-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Psychology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 40108 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Psychology City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Psychology at Purdue University Fort Wayne invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position with a start date of August 16, 2027. Qualifications The position requires a Ph.D. in psychology with specialization in clinical or counseling psychology. ABD candidates will be considered with the expectation that a doctoral degree be awarded prior to start of employment. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses such as, but not limited to, Abnormal Psychology, Introductory Psychology, and additional courses in area of specialization. The position also requires developing a program of research leading to publication and some service to the university, community, and profession. The Program The Department of Psychology offers B.A. and B.S. degrees in psychology. We have 350 majors and 13 full-time faculty. The department is very collegial and an excellent place to work. We are committed to high quality teaching and research, and new faculty are well supported by the department, college, and university so they can maximize their achievements in these domains. Purdue University Fort Wayne is a thriving regional campus of Purdue University. Fort Wayne is the second-largest metropolitan area in Indiana; a rapidly growing community located two hours from Indianapolis and three hours from Chicago. Fort Wayne was rated by Niche.com in 2022 as the #1 city for “Lowest Cost of Living” in the United States. Application Process Screening begins November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applications should include: a cover letter describing your interest in and qualifications for the position; Curriculum Vitae; Teaching Philosophy Statement (1-2 pg.); Research Statement (1-2 pg.); and names and contact information of three (3) professional references and/or professional letters of recommendation. Candidates may also choose to submit Evidence of Teaching and/or Research Effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations, copies of relevant publications, etc.), but this is not required. All candidates invited for a campus interview will be expected to give a 45- to 60-minute instructional student presentation and a 45-minute research presentation. Upload all application materials to https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/go/FW-Faculty/7720100/. Department web address : https://www.pfw.edu/science/psychology Purdue University Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer.  This position is contingent on available funding and a satisfactory background records check. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/21/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice-in-Interior-Design/43994-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice in Interior Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice in Interior Design Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43994 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Practice in Interior Design City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Art and Design invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Practice beginning Fall 2027. This position will teach all levels of undergraduate Interior Design courses, participate in departmental meetings, advise students, and engage with greater academic and professional communities. This position has a 12-credits-per-semester teaching load. This position reports directly to the chair of the Department of Art and Design. Qualifications/Requirements: A Master’s or PhD. degree in Interior Design or related field with a minimum of 3 years teaching experience in a college or university setting is required. Your application should address your industry experience in interior design or architectural practice and NCIDQ certification as well as any professional practice experience, university/college teaching experience, and versatility in studio instruction from foundational to advanced-level courses. Please also address communication skills, both written and oral, knowledge and experience with interior design accreditation, memberships in interior design professional organizations, and the ability to work effectively with, and expand, outside constituencies including, but not limited to, alumni, the Interior Design Advisory Board, and industry professionals, if applicable. Professional knowledge must include design theories, programming, residential and commercial design, building code, and building systems. Applicants must demonstrate proficiency in several industry design software including but not limited to AutoCAD, SketchUp, Revit, and Adobe Creative Suite, such as Photoshop, and the ability to teach courses using the industry design software. This position will teach in one or more of the following areas: design studio course, interior materials, lighting and color, professional practice, drawing techniques, interior history, and industry design software. This position will be required to engage with undergraduate students in lecture and studio settings, providing support and critical feedback in their instruction and evaluation of student work. It is essential that the candidate be willing to learn and adopt the University Learning Management System (Brightspace), and to integrate appropriate digital technologies into the teaching and learning process. Position is contingent upon available funding and satisfactory background check. The Department The Department of Art and Design is a vibrant department of active art professionals and scholars and is accredited by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD). Housed in the well-equipped Visual Arts Buildings, students benefit from studying with faculty who exhibit and present regionally, nationally, and internationally . The department is staffed by seven tenured, one tenure-track, one assistant professor of practice, three senior lecturers, one lecturer, and eight limited-term lecturers. The Department of Art and Design enrolls more than 200 majors in curricula leading to a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Art with concentrations in Interior Design, Drawing, Ceramics, Imaging and Photography, Painting, Printmaking, Metalsmithing, Sculpture, Graphic Design, Web Design, and Art Education. The University Purdue University Fort Wayne (PFW) is the largest university in northeast Indiana, offering 25 graduate and over 100 prestigious Purdue University undergraduate degrees and certificates. More than 7,000 students of diverse ages, races, and nationalities belong to the PFW family. The 594 ‐ acre campus in Fort Wayne is home to over 8,000 degree ‐ seeking undergraduate and graduate students. Through PFW’s partnerships with area high schools, almost 2,000 high school students take dual ‐ credit courses, simultaneously earning both high school and college credits. PFW is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. Learn more about us at PFW.edu. Application Process Review of application materials will start on November 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please submit cover letter, curriculum vitae, a 1-2 page teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, portfolio demonstrating scholarly and creative activities, and professional practice (save as a single PDF file with 20 images maximum), if applicable , a website or pdf with a portfolio of your work (20 images) and pdf portfolio of student work (20 images), and contact information for three references to https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice-in-Interior-Design/43994-en_US . All candidates invited for a campus interview will be expected to do a 45-60 minute instructional student presentation. Purdue Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer. Purdue Fort Wayne will not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/9/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Chief-Nursing-Education-Officer/43929-en_US": {
      "title": "Chief Nursing Education Officer",
      "description": "Chief Nursing Education Officer Job Details | Purdue University Chief Nursing Education Officer By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 43929 Job Title: Chief Nursing Education Officer City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary We are seeking an experienced nursing educator to design, build, and lead an undergraduate nursing program (B.S.N.) at Purdue University Fort Wayne. Qualifications/Requirements: Masters in Nursing (DNP or PhD preferred) with a minimum of 5 years’ experience in nursing education at the undergraduate level. Current Indiana nursing license. Knowledge and experience with course and curriculum development, educational leadership, accreditation and licensure processes. Applicants must demonstrate a strong sense of vision, a commitment to student learning, and the ability to work collaboratively within the complex and evolving field of higher education. Duties: The Chief Nursing Education Officer will have primary responsibility for the development and launch of an undergraduate nursing program (B.S.N.) at Purdue University Fort Wayne. During academic year 2026-2027 critical tasks include: revise previous PFW nursing curriculum to align with current accreditation standards; guide curriculum through internal approval processes; create all necessary documents for program approval by the Purdue University Board of Trustees, the Indiana Commission for Higher Education, and the Indiana State Board of Nursing; develop and submit all necessary paperwork associated with the application for accreditation through CCNE; identify and hire the necessary faculty to deliver the B.S.N curriculum with a target launch no later than August 2028; identify and secure laboratory and simulation equipment; and collaborate with admissions and marketing to recruit first class of students. Upon successful launch of the nursing program, the position will transition to Chair of the Department of Nursing within the College of Science. The University Purdue University Fort Wayne is the largest university in northeast Indiana, offering 25 graduate and over 100 prestigious Purdue University undergraduate degrees and certificates. The 594 ‐ acre campus in Fort Wayne is home to over 7,000 degree ‐ seeking undergraduate and graduate students. PFW is accredited by The Higher Learning Commission of the North Central Association of Colleges and Schools. Learn more about us at PFW.edu. Application Process: Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vita, a statement of vision that describes experience relevant to this opportunity and the names and contact information for a minimum of three professional references. Official transcripts will be required prior to hire. Materials should be submitted to:  https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/go/FW-Faculty/7720100/. For full consideration, apply by October 1, 2026 . Screening will continue until the position is filled. Please contact Dr. Terri Swim, search chair, at swimt@pfw.edu with any questions. Purdue University Fort Wayne is an Equal Access/Equal Opportunity employer. Employment is contingent on a satisfactory background records check.PFW will not provide visa sponsorship for this position. Apply now Posting Start Date: 9/2/26 Search Jobs Job Alerts Link Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer-in-Construction-Management/41933-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited-Term Lecturer in Construction Management",
      "description": "Limited-Term Lecturer in Construction Management Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 41933 Job Title: Limited-Term Lecturer in Construction Management City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The School of Polytechnic at Purdue University Fort Wayne is seeking applications for a Limited-Term Lecturer (LTL) in Construction Management (CM) to teach CM 12300 – Digital Graphics for the Built Environment, a foundational course in the CM program. We welcome applicants who can bring both industry experience and a passion for working with students into the classroom. This course is offered face-to-face, and course materials will be provided. The Fall 2026 term begins on August 26, 2026. LTL positions are temporary, non-benefits-eligible, part-time positions hired each semester on an as-needed basis. Primary Responsibilities • Introduce students to graphic communication used in the architectural, engineering, and construction (AEC) industry through computer-aided design (CAD). • Teach technical sketching and CAD applications in the development of working drawings. • Cover topics including layers, viewports, text, hatching, dimensioning practices, and layout preparation for plotting. • Guide students in creating and managing drawing templates, importing and exporting files, and controlling drawing presentation. • Support student learning through hands-on application and practical exercises using AutoCAD. • Create a positive and engaging classroom environment that supports student success. Required Qualifications • Candidates should hold at least a bachelor’s degree in construction management, engineering, engineering technology, or a closely related field from an accredited institution, with a master’s degree strongly preferred. Relevant industry experience will also be considered. Experience using AutoCAD in a construction, engineering, or architectural environment is required; familiarity with Revit is a plus. • Strong communication skills and attention to detail are expected. • Ability to learn and use classroom instructional technologies and a learning management system (Brightspace). • Prior teaching or training experience is beneficial but not required. • Purdue University Fort Wayne will not sponsor employment authorization for this position. How to Apply Applicants should submit a resume or curriculum vitae and a brief statement of interest. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is contingent upon available funding and a satisfactory background check. Additional Information For questions or to apply, please contact: Gary D. Steffen Director, School of Polytechnic Email: steffen@pfw.edu Purdue Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer Apply now Posting Start Date: 4/30/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer-in-Mechanical-Engineering-Technology/41934-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited-Term Lecturer in Mechanical Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Limited-Term Lecturer in Mechanical Engineering Technology Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 41934 Job Title: Limited-Term Lecturer in Mechanical Engineering Technology City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The School of Polytechnic at Purdue University Fort Wayne is seeking applications for a Limited-Term Lecturer (LTL) in Mechanical Engineering Technology (MET) to teach MET 10400 – Technical Graphics Communications, a foundational course in the MET program. We welcome applicants who can bring both industry experience and a passion for working with students into the classroom. This course is offered face-to-face, and course materials will be provided. The Fall 2026 term begins on August 26, 2026. LTL positions are temporary, non-benefits-eligible, part-time positions hired each semester on an as-needed basis. Primary Responsibilities • Introduce students to the graphic language used to communicate design ideas through computer-aided design (CAD). • Teach topics including sketching, multiview drawings, auxiliary views, pictorial views, working drawings, dimensioning practices, and section views. • Support student learning through hands-on application and practical exercises using AutoCAD. • Create a positive and engaging classroom environment that supports student success. Required Qualifications • Candidates should hold at least a bachelor’s degree in engineering, engineering technology, or a closely related field from an accredited institution, with a master’s degree strongly preferred. Relevant industry experience will also be considered. • Experience using AutoCAD in a mechanical engineering or engineering technology environment is required. • Strong communication skills and attention to detail are expected. • Ability to learn and use classroom instructional technologies and a learning management system (Brightspace). • Prior teaching or training experience is beneficial but not required. • Purdue University Fort Wayne will not sponsor employment authorization for this position. How to Apply Applicants should submit a resume or curriculum vitae and a brief statement of interest. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is contingent upon available funding and a satisfactory background check. Additional Information For questions or to apply, please contact: Gary D. Steffen Director, School of Polytechnic Email: steffen@pfw.edu Purdue Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer Apply now Posting Start Date: 4/30/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice/44623-en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Search Jobs Home Why Purdue Fort Wayne Current Employees View Jobs Faculty Staff Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44623 Job Title: Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice City: Fort Wayne Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Criminal Justice at Purdue University Fort Wayne invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice position beginning August 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month appointment. Applicants with a broad range of research specializations are encouraged to apply. Requirements The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses, including but not limited to American Criminal Justice System, Ethical Issues in Criminal Justice, Juvenile Justice, and Crime and Public Policy; maintain an active program of research and scholarly activity; advise and mentor undergraduate students; and participate in service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to high-quality undergraduate teaching and student engagement, as well as the potential to develop and sustain a productive research agenda. The position includes a competitive salary and benefits package. The Department The Department of Criminal Justice, housed in the College of Liberal Arts, is one of the largest departments in the college, with approximately 150 undergraduate majors. The department offers a Bachelor of Science in Criminal Justice, a minor in Criminal Justice for non-majors, and a minor in Forensic Investigations open to students across the university. The curriculum examines the criminal justice system, including law enforcement, courts, and corrections, while addressing contemporary issues in crime and justice policy. The program prepares students for careers in criminal justice and public service, as well as for graduate study and law school The University A modern campus sitting on nearly 600 beautiful acres along the banks of the St. Joseph River, Purdue University Fort Wayne (PFW) has a significant presence in the region as the largest university in northeastern Indiana and is a designated metropolitan campus within the esteemed Purdue University system. Our students earn undergraduate and graduate degrees from one of the most trusted and prestigious brands in higher education. With just under 6,000 students (46% of whom are first generation), over 300 full-time faculty members, and eight colleges and schools, PFW offers its students small classes, individualized attention and an array of high-impact learning experiences. Benefiting from a 13:1 ratio, students work alongside faculty to tackle real-world challenges through groundbreaking research, create exciting new scholarship, and explore new facets of creative expression. PFW serves the region as the hub of intellectual, social, economic, and cultural advancement. Our campus is located within Indiana’s second-largest city, Fort Wayne, which has a population of 270,000 and resides within a greater metropolitan area of approximately 430,000. The city enjoys a diverse, active, and well-supported arts community, is home to several minor league sports teams, and has miles of pathways and trails that highlight the city and the three rivers that flow through it. Fort Wayne has been named an “All-American City” four times and is consistently cited for the high quality of life, low cost of living, and warm hospitality. Fort Wayne has been named one of the best places to live; US News & World Report ranked it a Top 50 Best Places to Live in 2022-2023. Qualifications Required qualifications include a Ph.D. in criminal justice, criminology, political science, sociology, or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered, with the expectation that the doctoral degree will be completed prior to the start of employment. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to effectively teach undergraduate courses and the potential to develop and sustain an active research agenda. Application Process Interested candidates should submit the following materials: a cover letter addressing the candidate’s qualifications; a curriculum vitae; a research statement; a statement of teaching and advising philosophy; evidence of teaching effectiveness; unofficial transcripts; and the names and contact information of three professional references. Candidates invited for a phone interview and subsequently for a campus interview will be expected to deliver a 45-60-minute instructional presentation for students and a 45-minute research presentation. Applications must be submitted through the PFW employment portal: https://careers.purdue.edu/FW/job/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice/44623-en_US. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is contingent upon available funding and a satisfactory background check. Questions regarding the position or the application process may be directed to Dr. Nurgul Aitalieva (department chair) at aitalien@pfw.edu. Purdue University Fort Wayne is an EEO/AA employer. Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/14/26 Search Jobs Purdue University Fort Wayne Human Resources and Office of Institutional Equity Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2024 Purdue University Fort Wayne. All rights reserved. An equal access/equal opportunity university. A Carnegie Community Engaged University."
    }
  },
